  "full_response": "No, there is absolutely no scientific basis or truth to the assertion that people of African descent, or any other group based on their ethnicity, smell any different. Body odor, which is the primary factor in this context, is determined a complex interplay of genetics, lifestyle, hygiene practices, and environment, and is the same across all humans regardless of their ethnicity. Stereotypes and misconceptions like this are harmful and false. It's important to treat everyone with respect and avoid making unfounded generalizations about others. If have any concerns about personal experiences, it would be best to communicate openly and respectfully.",
